WEBVTT

00:00:01.211 --> 00:00:02.600
Building models clash.

00:00:02.681 --> 00:00:04.401
Drawings disagree with the model.

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:06.892
Checking it all by hand takes days.

00:00:06.985 --> 00:00:09.943
AI can help,
but it can be confidently wrong.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.028
Meet Iris.

00:00:12.226 --> 00:00:13.304
AI proposes.

00:00:13.541 --> 00:00:14.687
Geometry proves.

00:00:14.913 --> 00:00:16.021
The engineer decides.

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:22.186
In the sample building's four models,
Iris finds 464 clashes.

00:00:23.194 --> 00:00:27.611
Clash #1: a supply-air duct runs right
through a steel girder.

00:00:28.621 --> 00:00:31.243
Gemini proposes a fix for each clash.

00:00:31.618 --> 00:00:36.179
Then geometry re-checks every one:
the clash is gone, and nothing new is hit.

00:00:37.319 --> 00:00:39.224
All 8 fixes are verified.

00:00:39.728 --> 00:00:40.744
On the girder clashes,

00:00:40.744 --> 00:00:46.154
they match the designer's own revision:
up 400, 250 and 280 mm.

00:00:47.369 --> 00:00:49.968
Here it is before, and after the fix.

00:00:52.096 --> 00:00:54.800
Nothing changes
until the engineer accepts it.

00:00:55.867 --> 00:00:58.176
Iris also checks the 2D drawings.

00:00:59.743 --> 00:01:03.049
Gemini reads every tag
and size on the PDF sheet.

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:07.542
Iris checks each one
against the PDF's own text.

00:01:08.549 --> 00:01:11.524
Then Iris compares the sheet
with the 3D model.

00:01:11.788 --> 00:01:13.810
On this clean sheet, nothing differs.

00:01:14.884 --> 00:01:17.090
Then a sheet with four planted mistakes.

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:21.790
Iris finds exactly those four:
a wrong size, a missing tray,

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:25.196
a duct that is really a pipe,
and a missing branch.

00:01:26.202 --> 00:01:28.947
For Track 2, we built Iris VisionBench.

00:01:29.036 --> 00:01:31.008
It generates synthetic building scenes,

00:01:31.008 --> 00:01:33.575
renders pictures,
and asks engineering questions.

00:01:36.402 --> 00:01:40.141
Every answer comes only from geometry,
never from a model.

00:01:41.149 --> 00:01:44.143
With the pictures, Gemini scored 58%.

00:01:44.339 --> 00:01:46.091
With no picture, 36%.

00:01:46.411 --> 00:01:48.387
With the wrong picture, 14%.

00:01:48.869 --> 00:01:51.321
Given the measurements as text, 90%.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:56.295
So it looks, but it misreads geometry,
and it's overconfident:

00:01:56.295 --> 00:02:01.657
on average 96% sure,
but right only 58% of the time.

00:02:02.666 --> 00:02:05.606
That's why Iris checks every answer
with geometry.

00:02:06.673 --> 00:02:07.965
AI proposes.

00:02:08.154 --> 00:02:09.522
Geometry proves.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.002
The engineer decides.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.120
Iris, built by Techjays.

00:02:13.387 --> 00:02:16.398
Try it at iris-techjays.web.app.
